        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "greg",
            "am"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "greg (flock) and am (friend)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "cord",
            "sent"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "cord (heart) and sent (feel)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>gregarious</b><br>fond of company; sociable",
            "<b>greg</b> <i>flock</i> + -arious<br>→ “of the flock (sociable)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>segregate</b><br>to set apart from others",
            "se- <i>apart</i> + <b>greg</b> <i>flock</i> + -ate<br>→ “set apart from the flock”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>egregious</b><br>outstandingly bad; shocking",
            "e- <i>out</i> + <b>greg</b> <i>flock</i> + -ious<br>→ “standing out from the flock”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>aggregate</b><br>a whole formed by combining many parts; a total",
            "ag- <i>toward</i> + <b>greg</b> <i>flock</i> + -ate<br>→ “flocked together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>amicable</b><br>friendly and without quarrels",
            "<b>amic</b> <i>friend</i> + -able<br>→ “friendly”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>inimical</b><br>harmful; unfriendly",
            "in- <i>not</i> + <b>imic</b> <i>friend</i> + -al<br>→ “not friendly”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>accord</b><br>agreement; harmony",
            "ac- <i>to</i> + <b>cord</b> <i>heart</i><br>→ “heart to heart”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>discord</b><br>disagreement; lack of harmony",
            "dis- <i>apart</i> + <b>cord</b> <i>heart</i><br>→ “hearts apart”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>consensus</b><br>general agreement",
            "con- <i>together</i> + <b>sens</b> <i>feel</i> + -us<br>→ “feeling together”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dissent</b><br>disagreement with an official or common view",
            "dis- <i>apart</i> + <b>sent</b> <i>feel</i><br>→ “feeling apart”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "A word that changed sides",
        "q": "The referee made an <b>egregious</b> error and gave the goal to the wrong team. What does <i>egregious</i> mean today, and what did it once mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>e-</b> (out) + <b>greg</b> (flock) + <b>-ious</b>: “standing out from the flock.”",
          "At first that was praise: an egregious scholar stood out from the crowd.",
          "Over time, people used it mostly for things that stand out in a bad way."
        ],
        "a": "Today: outstandingly bad; shocking. Once: outstanding in a good way."
      },
