      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "Missing <b>am</b> when it changes shape. In <b>inimical</b> (harmful, unfriendly), the Latin <i>amicus</i> (friend) became <i>-imic-</i> after <i>in-</i>: “not friendly.” The same change made <i>enemy</i>, which came to English through French. And remember that <b>egregious</b> now means bad, even though it once meant good."
